k to the White king on e1)\n- White must respond to the check, giving Black the initiative\n- After White blocks or moves the king, Black can continue developing while White's advanced knights lack proper support\n- This creates immediate tactical complications favoring the side with the initiative\n- It's a principled developing move that doesn't waste time\n\n**Answer:** B: f8-b4"}
