thout development and proper king safety.\n\nReason: Castling kingside is the strongest move here. It addresses the most critical need - king safety - while also activating my h8 rook and completing a fundamental opening principle. With White having an active knight on e5, keeping my king in the center is risky. After castling, I can then focus on developing my remaining pieces and challenging White's center.\n\nAnswer: K: e8-g8"}
